style=\"background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255); color: inherit; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px; font-variant-ligatures: inherit; font-variant-caps: inherit;\">What makes a good real estate investment? Any good investment has a high chance of success and a solid return on your investment. One of the factors in favor of real estate investing is the relatively small stake needed to get started, compared to investing in many other assets.</span></div></div></div></div><div id=\"article-body_1-0\" class=\"comp article-body mntl-block\" data-contain-tooltips=\"true\" style=\"position: relative;\"><div id=\"mntl-sc-page_1-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-page mntl-block article-body-content\" data-sc-sticky-offset=\"80\" data-sc-ad-label-height=\"0\" data-sc-ad-track-spacing=\"90\" data-sc-min-track-height=\"250\" data-sc-max-track-height=\"600\" data-sc-breakpoint=\"50em\" data-sc-load-immediate=\"1\" data-sc-content-positions=\"[300, 1, 1, 1250, 1, 1, 1, 1]\" data-bind-scroll-on-start=\"true\"><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_2-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_3-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">A home&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/mortgage.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"1\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">mortgage</a>&nbsp;generally requires a 20% to 25% down payment, but, in some cases, a 5% down payment is all it takes to purchase an entire property as a rental opportunity. That\'s great for those with do-it-yourself skills and plenty of spare time, but it\'s only one of several ways to make money in real estate without an outsized investment upfront. These are some other real estate investment strategies to consider, along with their pros and cons.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_4-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div></div></div></div></h1><h3 class=\"mntl-sc-block-universal-callout__heading\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 16px; letter-spacing: 0.05rem; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 1.5625rem 1.25rem 0.5625rem; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif;\">KEY TAKEAWAYS</h3><h1 class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\"><div class=\"loc article-content\" style=\"font-weight: 400; grid-area: content; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px;\"><div class=\"comp article-body mntl-block\" data-contain-tooltips=\"true\" style=\"position: relative;\"><div class=\"comp mntl-sc-page mntl-block article-body-content\" data-sc-sticky-offset=\"80\" data-sc-ad-label-height=\"0\" data-sc-ad-track-spacing=\"90\" data-sc-min-track-height=\"250\" data-sc-max-track-height=\"600\" data-sc-breakpoint=\"50em\" data-sc-load-immediate=\"1\" data-sc-content-positions=\"[300, 1, 1, 1250, 1, 1, 1, 1]\" data-bind-scroll-on-start=\"true\"><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_5-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-callout--whatyouneedtoknow finance-sc-block-callout mntl-sc-block-universal-callout theme-whatyouneedtoknow\" data-tracking-id=\"mntl-sc-block-callout\" data-tracking-container=\"true\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 1rem 0px 2rem; position: relative;\"><div class=\"mntl-sc-block-universal-callout__body\" style=\"padding: 0px 1.25rem 1.25rem;\"><ul style=\"margin-bottom: 0px; padding-left: 1.5rem; list-style-position: initial; list-style-image: initial;\"><li style=\"padding-bottom: 0.375rem;\">Buying and managing rental property is an option for investors with do-it-yourself skills and the time to manage the property hands-on.</li><li style=\"padding-bottom: 0.375rem;\">\"Flippers\" look for undervalued properties and look to sell them quickly for a profit.</li><li style=\"padding-bottom: 0.375rem;\">REIGs are an option for passive investing in real estate.</li><li style=\"padding-bottom: 0.375rem;\">REITs pay dividends and can be bought and sold on exchanges, like stocks.</li><li style=\"padding-bottom: 0.375rem; margin-bottom: 0px;\">Online real estate investing platforms offer diverse opportunities for a relatively modest stake.</li></ul></div></div><span class=\"heading-toc\" id=\"toc-1-rental-properties\"></span></div></div></div></h1><h2 id=\"mntl-sc-block_6-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-heading mntl-sc-block-heading\" style=\"font-size: 26px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(17, 17, 17); overflow-wrap: break-word; margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif;\"><span class=\"mntl-sc-block-heading__text\">1. Rental Properties</span></h2><h1 class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\"><div class=\"loc article-content\" style=\"font-weight: 400; grid-area: content; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px;\"><div class=\"comp article-body mntl-block\" data-contain-tooltips=\"true\" style=\"position: relative;\"><div class=\"comp mntl-sc-page mntl-block article-body-content\" data-sc-sticky-offset=\"80\" data-sc-ad-label-height=\"0\" data-sc-ad-track-spacing=\"90\" data-sc-min-track-height=\"250\" data-sc-max-track-height=\"600\" data-sc-breakpoint=\"50em\" data-sc-load-immediate=\"1\" data-sc-content-positions=\"[300, 1, 1, 1250, 1, 1, 1, 1]\" data-bind-scroll-on-start=\"true\"><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_7-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">Owning&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/residentialrentalproperty.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"1\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">rental properties</a>&nbsp;is a good choice for individuals who have do-it-yourself (DIY) skills, the patience to manage tenants, and the time to do the job properly.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_8-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_9-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">Although financing can be obtained with a relatively low down payment, it does require substantial cash on hand to finance upfront maintenance and to cover periods when the property is empty or tenants do not pay their rent.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_10-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_11-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">On the plus side, once the property starts bringing in cash, it can be leveraged to acquire more property. Gradually, the investor can acquire a number of income streams from multiple properties, offsetting unexpected costs and losses with new income.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_12-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div></div></div></div></h1><h3 class=\"mntl-sc-block__heading mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__heading\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 26px; flex: 0 0 100%; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif;\">Rental Property Investing</h3><h1 class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\"><div class=\"loc article-content\" style=\"font-weight: 400; grid-area: content; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px;\"><div class=\"comp article-body mntl-block\" data-contain-tooltips=\"true\" style=\"position: relative;\"><div class=\"comp mntl-sc-page mntl-block article-body-content\" data-sc-sticky-offset=\"80\" data-sc-ad-label-height=\"0\" data-sc-ad-track-spacing=\"90\" data-sc-min-track-height=\"250\" data-sc-max-track-height=\"600\" data-sc-breakpoint=\"50em\" data-sc-load-immediate=\"1\" data-sc-content-positions=\"[300, 1, 1, 1250, 1, 1, 1, 1]\" data-bind-scroll-on-start=\"true\"><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_13-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-comparisonlist mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; display: flex; flex-flow: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 24px;\"><div class=\"mntl-sc-block__wrapper mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__wrapper\" style=\"flex-grow: 0; border: 1px solid rgb(44, 64, 208); padding: 24px; box-shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) 0px 1px 3px; flex-basis: 47%;\"><span class=\"mntl-sc-block__list-heading mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__list-heading\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.25px;\">Pros</span><ul class=\"mntl-sc-block__list mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__list\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; padding-left: 1.5rem; list-style-position: initial; list-style-image: initial;\"><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem;\">Provides regular income and potential appreciation</p></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem;\">Can be maximized through leverage</p></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px;\">Many expenses are tax-deductible</p></li></ul></div><div class=\"mntl-sc-block__wrapper mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__wrapper\" style=\"flex-grow: 0; border: 1px solid rgb(44, 64, 208); padding: 24px; box-shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) 0px 1px 3px; flex-basis: 47%;\"><span class=\"mntl-sc-block__list-heading mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__list-heading\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.25px;\">Cons</span><ul class=\"mntl-sc-block__list mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__list\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; padding-left: 1.5rem; list-style-position: initial; list-style-image: initial;\"><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem;\">Managing tenants can be tedious</p></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem;\">Unexpected costs can eat up income</p></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px;\">Unpredictable vacancies can reduce income</p></li></ul></div></div><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_14-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><div id=\"native_1-0\" class=\"comp native mm-ads-native \" data-right-rail-index=\"3\" style=\"width: 596px; height: auto; --native-ad-height: auto;\"><div id=\"mm-ads-native__adunit_1-0\" class=\"comp mm-ads-native__adunit mm-ads-gpt-dynamic-adunit mm-ads-gpt-adunit scads-to-load gpt native dynamic js-lazy-ad is-requested\" style=\"text-align: center; min-height: 286px;\"><div id=\"native\" class=\"wrapper\" data-timed-refresh=\"30000\" data-type=\"native\" data-pos=\"native\" data-priority=\"4\" data-sizes=\"[[1, 3],&quot;fluid&quot;]\" data-rtb=\"false\" data-wait-for-third-party=\"false\" data-targeting=\"{}\"><div id=\"sidebar-overlay\"></div></div></div></div></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_15-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">According to&nbsp;U.S. Census Bureau data, the sales prices of new homes (a rough indicator for real estate values)&nbsp;consistently increased in value from the 1960s to 2007, before dipping during the financial crisis.<span class=\"mntl-inline-citation mntl-dynamic-tooltip--trigger wrapped\" data-id=\"#citation-8\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"position: inherit; padding-bottom: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 238); cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; justify-content: center; align-items: baseline; margin-left: 2px; letter-spacing: 0.07em; line-height: 1;\"><span style=\"pointer-events: none; position: relative; z-index: 89; top: -7px;\">1</span></span>&nbsp;Subsequently, sales prices resumed their ascent, even surpassing pre-crisis levels.<span class=\"mntl-inline-citation mntl-dynamic-tooltip--trigger wrapped\" data-id=\"#citation-6\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"position: inherit; padding-bottom: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 238); cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; justify-content: center; align-items: baseline; margin-left: 2px; letter-spacing: 0.07em; line-height: 1;\"><span style=\"pointer-events: none; position: relative; z-index: 89; top: -7px;\">2</span></span><span class=\"mntl-inline-citation mntl-dynamic-tooltip--trigger wrapped\" data-id=\"#citation-5\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"position: inherit; padding-bottom: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 238); cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; justify-content: center; align-items: baseline; margin-left: 2px; letter-spacing: 0.07em; line-height: 1;\"><span style=\"pointer-events: none; position: relative; z-index: 89; top: -7px;\">3</span></span></p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_16-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_17-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">By the end of 2023, the average home sale price in the U.S. hit $498,300, slightly off record highs recorded earlier in the year.<span class=\"mntl-inline-citation mntl-dynamic-tooltip--trigger wrapped\" data-id=\"#citation-10\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"position: inherit; padding-bottom: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 238); cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; justify-content: center; align-items: baseline; margin-left: 2px; letter-spacing: 0.07em; line-height: 1;\"><span style=\"pointer-events: none; position: relative; z-index: 89; top: -7px;\">4</span></span></p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_18-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div></div></div></div></h1><h3 class=\"mntl-sc-block-universal-callout__heading\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0.5313rem; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600; padding-left: 2rem; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.75px; text-transform: uppercase;\">WARNING</h3><h1 class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\"><div class=\"loc article-content\" style=\"font-weight: 400; grid-area: content; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px;\"><div class=\"comp article-body mntl-block\" data-contain-tooltips=\"true\" style=\"position: relative;\"><div class=\"comp mntl-sc-page mntl-block article-body-content\" data-sc-sticky-offset=\"80\" data-sc-ad-label-height=\"0\" data-sc-ad-track-spacing=\"90\" data-sc-min-track-height=\"250\" data-sc-max-track-height=\"600\" data-sc-breakpoint=\"50em\" data-sc-load-immediate=\"1\" data-sc-content-positions=\"[300, 1, 1, 1250, 1, 1, 1, 1]\" data-bind-scroll-on-start=\"true\"><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_19-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-callout mntl-sc-block-universal-callout theme-warning finance-sc-block-callout--generic\" data-tracking-id=\"mntl-sc-block-callout\" data-tracking-container=\"true\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; margin: 48px 0px; position: relative; border: 1px solid rgb(225, 226, 230); padding: 1rem;\"><div class=\"mntl-sc-block-universal-callout__body\" style=\"padding-left: 0px; line-height: 1.75;\"><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px;\">Mortgage lending discrimination is illegal.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/housing-discrimination-what-can-you-do-5074478\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"1\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">If you think you\'ve been discriminated against</a>&nbsp;based on race, religion, sex, marital status, use of public assistance, national origin, disability, or age, there are steps you can take. One such step is to file a report to the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.consumerfinance.gov/complaint/\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"externalLink\" data-ordinal=\"2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">Consumer Financial Protection Bureau</a>&nbsp;or with the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.hud.gov/program_offices/fair_housing_equal_opp/online-complaint\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"externalLink\" data-ordinal=\"3\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">U.S. Department of Housing and Urban Development (HUD)</a>.<span class=\"mntl-inline-citation mntl-dynamic-tooltip--trigger wrapped\" data-id=\"#citation-7\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"position: inherit; padding-bottom: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 238); cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; justify-content: center; align-items: baseline; margin-left: 2px; letter-spacing: 0.07em; line-height: 1;\"><span style=\"pointer-events: none; position: relative; z-index: 89; top: -7px;\">5</span></span></p></div><div id=\"finance-sc-block-callout__icon-container_1-0\" class=\"comp finance-sc-block-callout__icon-container mntl-block\" style=\"display: flex; position: absolute; justify-content: center; align-items: center; top: 1rem; left: 1rem; width: 1.25rem; height: 1.25rem;\"><svg class=\"icon finance-sc-block-callout__icon--warning \"><use xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" xlink:href=\"#finance-sc-block-callout__icon--warning\" href=\"#finance-sc-block-callout__icon--warning\"></use></svg></div></div><span class=\"heading-toc\" id=\"toc-2-real-estate-investment-groups-reigs\"></span></div></div></div></h1><h2 id=\"mntl-sc-block_20-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-heading mntl-sc-block-heading\" style=\"font-size: 26px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(17, 17, 17); overflow-wrap: break-word; margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif;\"><span class=\"mntl-sc-block-heading__text\">2. Real Estate Investment Groups (REIGs)</span></h2><h1 class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\"><div class=\"loc article-content\" style=\"font-weight: 400; grid-area: content; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px;\"><div class=\"comp article-body mntl-block\" data-contain-tooltips=\"true\" style=\"position: relative;\"><div class=\"comp mntl-sc-page mntl-block article-body-content\" data-sc-sticky-offset=\"80\" data-sc-ad-label-height=\"0\" data-sc-ad-track-spacing=\"90\" data-sc-min-track-height=\"250\" data-sc-max-track-height=\"600\" data-sc-breakpoint=\"50em\" data-sc-load-immediate=\"1\" data-sc-content-positions=\"[300, 1, 1, 1250, 1, 1, 1, 1]\" data-bind-scroll-on-start=\"true\"><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_21-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\"><a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/r/reig.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"1\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">Real estate investment groups</a>&nbsp;(REIGs) are ideal for people who have some capital and want to own rental real estate without the hassles of hands-on management.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_22-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_23-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">REIGs are a pool of money from a number of investors, similar to a small&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/m/mutualfund.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"1\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">mutual fund</a>, that is invested in rental properties.<span class=\"mntl-inline-citation mntl-dynamic-tooltip--trigger wrapped\" data-id=\"#citation-9\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"position: inherit; padding-bottom: 0px; vertical-align: baseline; font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 238); cursor: pointer; display: inline-flex; justify-content: center; align-items: baseline; margin-left: 2px; letter-spacing: 0.07em; line-height: 1;\"><span style=\"pointer-events: none; position: relative; z-index: 89; top: -7px;\">6</span></span>&nbsp;In a typical real estate investment group, a company buys or builds a set of apartment blocks or condos.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_24-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_25-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">A single investor can own one or multiple units of self-contained living space, but the company operating the investment group collectively manages all of the units, handling maintenance, advertising vacancies, and interviewing tenants.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_26-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_27-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">In exchange for conducting these management tasks, the company takes a percentage of the monthly rent.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_28-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_29-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">A standard real estate investment group&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/l/lease.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"1\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">lease</a>&nbsp;is in the investor’s name, and all of the units pool a portion of the rent to cover vacancies. This means you\'ll receive some income even if your unit is empty. As long as the vacancy rate for the pooled units doesn’t spike too high, there should be enough to cover costs.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_30-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div></div></div></div></h1><h3 class=\"mntl-sc-block__heading mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__heading\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: 26px; flex: 0 0 100%; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif;\">REIG Investing</h3><h1 class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\"><div class=\"loc article-content\" style=\"font-weight: 400; grid-area: content; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px;\"><div class=\"comp article-body mntl-block\" data-contain-tooltips=\"true\" style=\"position: relative;\"><div class=\"comp mntl-sc-page mntl-block article-body-content\" data-sc-sticky-offset=\"80\" data-sc-ad-label-height=\"0\" data-sc-ad-track-spacing=\"90\" data-sc-min-track-height=\"250\" data-sc-max-track-height=\"600\" data-sc-breakpoint=\"50em\" data-sc-load-immediate=\"1\" data-sc-content-positions=\"[300, 1, 1, 1250, 1, 1, 1, 1]\" data-bind-scroll-on-start=\"true\"><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_31-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-comparisonlist mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word; display: flex; flex-flow: wrap; gap: 1rem; margin-bottom: 24px;\"><div class=\"mntl-sc-block__wrapper mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__wrapper\" style=\"flex-grow: 0; border: 1px solid rgb(44, 64, 208); padding: 24px; box-shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) 0px 1px 3px; flex-basis: 47%;\"><span class=\"mntl-sc-block__list-heading mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__list-heading\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.25px;\">Pros</span><ul class=\"mntl-sc-block__list mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__list\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; padding-left: 1.5rem; list-style-position: initial; list-style-image: initial;\"><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem;\">More hands-off than owning rentals</p></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px;\">Provides income and appreciation</p></li></ul></div><div class=\"mntl-sc-block__wrapper mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__wrapper\" style=\"flex-grow: 0; border: 1px solid rgb(44, 64, 208); padding: 24px; box-shadow: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.15) 0px 1px 3px; flex-basis: 47%;\"><span class=\"mntl-sc-block__list-heading mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__list-heading\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 16px; font-weight: 700; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; letter-spacing: 0.25px;\">Cons</span><ul class=\"mntl-sc-block__list mntl-sc-block-universal-comparison-list__list\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; padding-left: 1.5rem; list-style-position: initial; list-style-image: initial;\"><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem;\">Vacancy risks</p></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem;\">Fees similar to those associated with mutual funds</p></li><li><p style=\"margin-bottom: 0px;\">Susceptible to unscrupulous managers</p></li></ul></div></div><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_32-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><span class=\"heading-toc\" id=\"toc-3-house-flipping\"></span></div></div></div></h1><h2 id=\"mntl-sc-block_33-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-heading mntl-sc-block-heading\" style=\"font-size: 26px; font-weight: 800; color: rgb(17, 17, 17); overflow-wrap: break-word; margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif;\"><span class=\"mntl-sc-block-heading__text\">3. House Flipping</span></h2><h1 class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\"><div class=\"loc article-content\" style=\"font-weight: 400; grid-area: content; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px;\"><div class=\"comp article-body mntl-block\" data-contain-tooltips=\"true\" style=\"position: relative;\"><div class=\"comp mntl-sc-page mntl-block article-body-content\" data-sc-sticky-offset=\"80\" data-sc-ad-label-height=\"0\" data-sc-ad-track-spacing=\"90\" data-sc-min-track-height=\"250\" data-sc-max-track-height=\"600\" data-sc-breakpoint=\"50em\" data-sc-load-immediate=\"1\" data-sc-content-positions=\"[300, 1, 1, 1250, 1, 1, 1, 1]\" data-bind-scroll-on-start=\"true\"><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_34-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">House flipping is for people with significant experience in real estate valuation, marketing, and renovation.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_35-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_36-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">This is the proverbial \"wild side\" of&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/articles/mortgages-real-estate/08/house-flip.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"1\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">real estate investing</a>. Just as&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/d/daytrader.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"2\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">day trading</a>&nbsp;is different from&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/b/buyandhold.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"3\" style=\"text-decoration-line: underline; color: rgb(44, 64, 208);\">buy-and-hold&nbsp;</a>investing, real estate flippers are distinct from buy-and-rent landlords.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_37-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_38-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">Real estate flippers often aim to profitably sell the undervalued properties they buy in less than six months.</p><div id=\"mntl-sc-block_39-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block mntl-sc-block-adslot mntl-block\" style=\"overflow-wrap: break-word;\"></div><p id=\"mntl-sc-block_40-0\" class=\"comp mntl-sc-block finance-sc-block-html mntl-sc-block-html\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1.75rem; overflow-wrap: break-word; counter-reset: section 0;\">Some property flippers don\'t invest in improving properties. They pick properties they hope have the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.investopedia.com/terms/i/intrinsicvalue.asp\" data-component=\"link\" data-source=\"inlineLink\" data-type=\"internalLink\" data-ordinal=\"1\" style=\"color: rgb(35, 51, 166);\">intrinsic value</a>&nbsp;needed to turn a profit without any alterations.</p></div></div></div></h1></header></div></div></div></div></section>', 'The Ultimate Guide to Real Estate Investment in 2023', '2025-06-20', 1, 'nice', '2025-06-03 08:58:45', '2025-06-04 04:42:34');
INSERT INTO `blogs` (`id`, `title`, `image`, `content`, `short_description`, `date`, `show_on_home`, `hashtags`, `created_at`, `updated_at`) VALUES
(6, '11 The Ultimate Guide to Real Estate Investment in 2023', 'blog/1748941136_photo-1600585154340-be6161a56a0c.jpg', '<section style=\"padding: 0px; margin: 0px 0px 30px; border: 0px; outline: none; list-style: none; text-size-adjust: none; appearance: none; float: left; width: 1905px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: &quot;Open Sans&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 10px;\"><div class=\"container\" style=\"padding: 0px 20px; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; border: 0px; outline: none; list-style: none; text-size-adjust: none; appearance: none; max-width: 1044px; width: 1044px;\"><div class=\"blogPostContainerDescription\" style=\"padding: 0px 30px 0px 0px; margin: 0px; border: 0px; outline: none; list-style: none; text-size-adjust: none; appearance: none; float: left; width: 702.797px;\"><div style=\"padding: 0px; margin: 0px; border: 0px; outline: none; list-style: none; text-size-adjust: none; appearance: none;\"><div class=\"loc article-pre-content\" style=\"grid-area: pre-content; color: rgb(17, 17, 17); font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; font-size: 18px; letter-spacing: 0.05px;\"><header id=\"article-header_1-0\" class=\"comp article-header mntl-block right-rail__offset js-toc-appear\" style=\"grid-area: header;\"><h1 id=\"article-heading_1-0\" class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px 0px 1rem; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\">5 Simple Ways to Invest in Real Estate</h1><h1 id=\"article-heading_1-0\" class=\"comp article-heading mntl-text-block\" style=\"margin-right: 0px; margin-bottom: 1rem; margin-left: 0px; font-family: Cabin-semi-bold, Cabin-fallback, sans-serif; font-size: 48px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.1;\"><div class=\"loc article-pre-content\" style=\"font-weight: 400; grid-area: pre-content; font-family: SourceSansPro, &quot;Source Sans Pro-fallback&quot;, sans-serif; fo